# Style Guide

## Color Usage
- Use color tokens from `app/globals.css` instead of hardcoded hex values when a token exists.
- Primary brand accent is `var(--color-brand-marigold)`.
- Primary text uses `var(--color-text)` and supporting text uses `var(--color-text-muted)`.
- Borders should use `var(--color-border)` unless a semantic support color is required.

## Surfaces And Shape
- Default card/background surface is white with subtle border contrast.
- Preferred card radii are between `10px` and `16px` for consistency across panels.
- Keep visual treatments clean and avoid heavy gradients unless a feature explicitly calls for it.

## Motion And Visual Density
- Use subtle animation that improves legibility, not decoration.
- Avoid visual clutter in utility panels; favor simple contrast and clear hierarchy.

## Audio Visualizer Styling
- Session monitor waveform should render mirrored pill-shaped bars with 19 total bars.
- Use vertical bars only; do not render horizontal guide lines.
- Waveform bars should use `var(--color-brand-marigold)` with restrained opacity changes for level feedback.
- Bars should be bottom-aligned and grow upward only from a shared baseline.
- The waveform should represent current-time speech energy (speech-reactive), not a timeline trail effect.
